From e1c70409578ea12037afd1180ba214e67757a8f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Feb 2026 14:08:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ccu: Add FUSA error handling and recovery support for CCU QUP

Add support for Functional Safety (FUSA) features in the QUP software
driver, including ECC, parity checks, and functional error detection
to meet automotive safety requirements.

Map FUSA fault aggregator registers for QUP instances using ioremap.
Enable FUSA block by configuring ECC and FUSA IRQ hardware registers
during initialization and power collapse scenarios.

Expose FUSA_IRQ_STATUS command to retrieve FUSA IRQ status for a given
QUP instance. Check all FUSA IRQ sets and return a 32-bit recovery mask
indicating required resets for SE and GPII nodes. Update CCU QUP config
structure to support QUP instance identification.

Report missing SE errors to the GENI I2C driver to improve error
visibility and handling.

Add synchronous logic to coordinate GPII reset requests with FUSA IRQ
and QUP functional reset operations. Track GPII state to prevent
repeated resets and ensure correct synchronization.

